WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
Geneva, 1559.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:08.030
The French Reformer John Calvin publishes
the final edition of his Institutes.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.930
In it, he defines predestination
as the eternal decree of God.

4
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:17.060
Some, Calvin writes, are
preordained to eternal life,

5
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.360
others to eternal damnation.

6
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.260
But if God chose who will be
saved before anyone was born,

7
00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.610
why pray, try, or blame anyone?

8
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.130
In this mission, you'll trace
the idea back to Augustine:

9
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.310
original sin, grace, and the Elect.

10
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.450
Then you'll test what
predestination means for blame,

11
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.170
for God's goodness, and for prayer.

12
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:44.000
Your mission: find out how believers
in predestination answer the question:

13
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.920
why pray, try, or blame anyone?
